.TH LEMMINGD 1 "September 2026" "lemmingd 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lemmingd \- selective local-development HTTP and HTTPS proxy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lemmingd
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lemmingd
routes configured domain and path combinations to local HTTP servers. It
intercepts HTTPS only for configured domains; all other CONNECT traffic is
tunneled unchanged. Exclusion prefixes take precedence over inclusion prefixes.
.PP
A unique local certificate authority is generated on first start. The CA is
not trusted or installed automatically.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " path"
Use the specified JSON configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-cacert " path"
Use the specified CA certificate file.
.TP
.BI \-cakey " path"
Use the specified CA private-key file.
.TP
.BI \-listen " host:port"
Override the configured listening address.
.TP
.B \-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lemmingd/config.json
Configuration and redirect rules. Defaults below
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lemmingd/ca.crt
Generated public CA certificate.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lemmingd/ca.key
Generated private CA key. Do not share this file.
.SH SECURITY
The default listener is 127.0.0.1:18080. Remote clients and non-loopback
redirect targets each require an explicit opt-in. Apply separate network access
controls before enabling either option.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hamsterd (1),
the project README, and SECURITY.md.
